title: Lio
act: Survey
location: Mill
scenario: The moving stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: not $saw_lio
---
Lio: You're the map maker. Can I see? Just the edge? #line:Lio.ef5a7949_0100_Lio
Lio: I make maps too. Of the mill, and the river. Grandmother taught me. She knew where everything was before. #line:Lio.ef5a7949_0200_Lio
Lio: The loft has the best view. You can see the whole bend of the river from up there. #line:Lio.ef5a7949_0300_Lio
===

title: Lio
act: Survey
location: Mill
scenario: The moving stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $saw_lio and $culprit == Culprit.Unknown
---
Lio: You saw me. Last night. Are you going to tell Maren? #line:Lio.28082e5d_0100_Lio
Lio: I'm not stealing land. I'm putting the stones back where they were. Grandmother said the true line runs under the hill, where the lantern folk are. #line:Lio.28082e5d_0200_Lio
Lio: Nobody believes her, because she's dead. #line:Lio.28082e5d_0300_Lio
-> Who are the lantern folk? #line:Lio.28082e5d_0400
    Lio: Lights, deep in the mine. The miners say so. Grandmother said they are the old border, written down. #line:Lio.28082e5d_0500_Lio
-> You can't go on moving them. #line:Lio.28082e5d_0600
    Lio: Then somebody should draw them where they belong. #line:Lio.28082e5d_0700_Lio
===

title: Lio
act: Survey
location: Mill
scenario: The moving stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $culprit != Culprit.Unknown
---
<<if $culprit == Culprit.Lio>>
    Lio: Maren came. Father shouted. The stones stay where they are now. #mood:angry #line:Lio.f5b2d696_0100_Lio
<<else>>
    Lio: They took the peddler in. Because of me. I didn't ask you to lie. #mood:sad #line:Lio.f5b2d696_0200_Lio
<<endif>>
===

title: Loft
act: All
location: Mill
quest: survey
---
<<if surveyed("loft")>>
    The loft is on your map. The river bends below, silver and slow. #line:Loft_0100
<<else>>
    You climb the ladder into the loft. From the hatch you see the whole bend of the river, and the stones along it. #line:Loft_0200
    <<survey loft>>
    <<detour SurveyCheck>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Sacks
act: All
location: Mill
scenario: The road
---
<<if $wheel_mended>>
    Sacks of fresh flour, still warm from the stones. #line:Sacks_0100
<<else>>
    Empty sacks. The mill has not ground for a week. #line:Sacks_0200
<<endif>>
===

title: Nan
act: Survey
location: Cottage
quest: herbs
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $quest_herbs == QuestState.NotStarted
---
Nan: Close the door, the warmth is getting out. I'm Nan. I make what the valley needs when it is ill. #line:Nan.49660c4c_0100_Nan
Nan: I'm short of three herbs for the spring. Nettle from the green, a dew-cup from the river, and hollyroot. Hedda has some in her cellar wall, though she doesn't know it. #line:Nan.49660c4c_0200_Nan
Nan: The dew-cup only opens in the morning, mind. And not for long now. Two mornings more, at most. #line:Nan.49660c4c_0300_Nan
-> I will bring them. #line:Nan.49660c4c_0400
    Nan: Good. I'll make you something for your trouble. #line:Nan.49660c4c_0500_Nan
    <<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Active>>
-> I have a map to make. #line:Nan.49660c4c_0600
    Nan: So you do. The herbs will wait. The dew-cups won't. #line:Nan.49660c4c_0700_Nan
    <<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Offered>>
<<quest_changed herbs>>
===

title: Nan
act: All
location: Cottage
quest: herbs
when: $quest_herbs == QuestState.Offered
---
Nan: Changed your mind about my herbs? #line:Nan.517b88a5_0100_Nan
-> Yes. Nettle, dew-cup, hollyroot. #line:Nan.517b88a5_0200
    Nan: You were listening. Go on, then. #line:Nan.517b88a5_0300_Nan
    <<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed herbs>>
-> Not yet. #line:Nan.517b88a5_0400
===

title: Nan
act: All
location: Cottage
quest: herbs
when: $quest_herbs == QuestState.Active
---
<<if has_item("nettle") and has_item("dewcup") and has_item("hollyroot")>>
    Nan: All three. And the dew-cup still wet. You have a good hand. #line:Nan.93e614c1_0100_Nan
    <<take nettle>>
    <<take dewcup>>
    <<take hollyroot>>
    Nan: Here. A remedy against the cold. Drink it before cold water, and the water won't stop your heart. #line:Nan.93e614c1_0200_Nan
    Nan: I don't know why a map maker would need it. But you will go places I don't. #line:Nan.93e614c1_0300_Nan
    <<give remedy>>
    <<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed herbs>>
<<else>>
    Nan: Still missing [plural value={3 - item_count("nettle") - item_count("dewcup") - item_count("hollyroot")} one="one herb" other="% herbs" /]. #line:Nan.93e614c1_0400_Nan
<<endif>>
===

title: Nan
act: All
location: Cottage
scenario: The moving stones
when: $quest_herbs != QuestState.Offered and $quest_herbs != QuestState.Active
when: $quest_herbs != QuestState.NotStarted or $act != Act.Survey
---
=> Nan: Lio's grandmother and I picked herbs together for forty years. She knew every stone in this valley. #line:Nan.87b42584_0100_Nan
=> Nan: The castle's steward came for a sleeping draught last month. I didn't ask what for. #line:Nan.87b42584_0200_Nan
=> Nan: You'll take a cold down there in the mine, if you go. Everyone does. <<if $act == Act.Castle>> #line:Nan.87b42584_0300_Nan
===

title: HerbTable
act: All
location: Cottage
quest: herbs
---
Jars and bunches on the table, each with a label in Nan's tidy hand. One jar is labelled "for the deep cold". #line:HerbTable_0100
===

title: Bell
act: All
location: Chapel
quest: survey
---
<<if surveyed("bell")>>
    The bell tower is on your map. The rope sways a little in the draught. #line:Bell_0100
<<else>>
    You climb the tower beside the bell rope. From the top the whole valley lies open, the castle, the mine, the abbey's meadows. #line:Bell_0200
    You take your bearings from the bell itself. #line:Bell_0300
    <<survey bell>>
    <<detour SurveyCheck>>
<<endif>>
===

title: MasonMark
act: All
location: Chapel
scenario: The moving stones
---
A mason's mark cut in the wall: a circle with a line through it, the same as on the boundary stones by the river. #line:MasonMark_0100
<<once>>
    Under it, almost worn away, words in the old tongue. "As above, so under the hill." #line:MasonMark_0200
<<endonce>>
===
